# Machine-local config for `task`. Copy and edit:
#
#   cp .env.example .env
#
# Loaded by task's `dotenv` from the root taskfile. A value here is a DEFAULT, not an
# override: `task build VITASDK=<path>` still wins. .env is fingerprinted by the build
# task, so editing it re-runs cmake.
#
# Every entry below is optional — leaving it commented out uses the built-in default.

# Where the vitasdk toolchain lives. CMakeLists.txt reads it from the environment and
# the portlib recipes put its bin/ on PATH. Default: ~/.local/opt/vitasdk
#
# Changing this means deleting build/ first: CMakeCache.txt pins absolute toolchain paths.
# VITASDK=/absolute/path/to/vitasdk
